cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code or the analyses it implements, please cite it.
title: >-
  An optimality tolerance, not the spacing of transcript-derived scores, selects the
  predicted metabolic exchanges in a weighted-parsimony model
abstract: >-
  Code, protocol records and result tables for a controlled study of the interface between
  transcript-derived reaction scores and constraint-based metabolic prediction. Measures how
  often rank-preserving changes to score spacing alter predicted extracellular exchange,
  locates the modeling stage at which the between-context variation is removed, sweeps the
  optimality tolerance that stage depends on, compares a bound-based interface and a published
  sampling workflow under the same evaluation, and tests the resulting reporting rule on an
  independent condition-response dataset.
